<urn:atm:triage:finding/AZS2-RBQA-002>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AZS2-RBQA-002" ;
  triage:title "boundary TOML review_gates have no mechanical enforcement; task_legacy_ops.rs ungoverned" ;
  triage:description "boundaries/atm-storage-rusqlite/async-task-mutation-store-sqlite.toml:42, boundaries/atm-storage/task-store.toml -- the 2026-09-10 fix attempt asserted 'lint_rules, not review_gates, are the mechanically enforced controls' but this claim is FALSE. Independent re-verification at QA-1 on PR #1382 (2026-09-10T03:45:00Z) against head 6937c547f2599ef548b98c52ae9d38456fd9f29c: (1) .just/lint_boundaries.py validates syntax only (line 1518-1521 validates identifier strings), never executes any named lint rule; (2) grep -rn LINT-BOUNDARY-ASYNC-TASK-MUTATION-SQLITE .just/ returns zero hits outside the TOML declaration itself; (3) the attempted fix made enforcement worse by claiming false mechanical enforcement in the TOML notes field. STILL OPEN -- boundary governance is not mechanically enforced. Source: QA-1 on PR #1382 (https://github.com/randlee/atm-core/pull/1382#issuecomment-5612459494). STILL OPEN at QA-2 (head b8900296c, independently confirmed by both arch-qa and ruthless-boundary-qa): the fix-3 pass corrected only 1 of 4 boundary TOMLs carrying the false claim -- boundaries/atm-storage/task-store.toml:41 now has honest wording, but the identical false claim remains verbatim in boundaries/atm-storage/async-task-mutation-store.toml:37 and boundaries/atm-storage-rusqlite/task-store-sqlite.toml:39, and boundaries/atm-storage-rusqlite/async-task-mutation-store-sqlite.toml:48 was reworded to a differently-phrased but equally false claim. Source: QA-2 on PR #1382. WORDING NOW FIXED at QA-3 (head 05e35a69716f9ef85bd7379d9a6ffb84553cfadf, independently confirmed by 4 reviewers): all 4 boundary TOMLs now carry byte-identical honest wording -- the false mechanical-enforcement claim is gone. STILL OPEN at QA-3, substantively: ruthless-boundary-qa traced one level deeper and found the underlying gap the false claim was papering over is unaddressed -- neither task-store-sqlite.toml's nor async-task-mutation-store-sqlite.toml's [enforcement].io_forbidden_source_modules lists the actual task-mutation writer modules (atm_storage_rusqlite::writer::task_ops, atm_storage_rusqlite::writer::task_legacy_ops), and implementation.module never resolves to those files either. The honest wording stopped the false claim but added no real mechanical coverage. Fix: populate [enforcement].io_forbidden_source_modules in both TOMLs naming those two modules, or narrow the io_forbidden claims to match actual scan scope. Source: QA-3 on PR #1382." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-az" ;
  triage:triageMode "followup_pass" ;
  triage:category "boundary-governance" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "boundaries/atm-storage-rusqlite/async-task-mutation-store-sqlite.toml, boundaries/atm-storage/task-store.toml, boundaries/atm-storage/async-task-mutation-store.toml, boundaries/atm-storage-rusqlite/task-store-sqlite.toml, .just/lint_boundaries.py" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-10T05:10:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AZ.2 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-09-10T02:11:59Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
